            "start_char": 27297
          },
          "confidence": 0.8,
          "entity_ids": [],
          "event_ids": [],
          "evidence_id": "sfev-3bfe9ccec611168f",
          "evidence_type": "inquiry_or_scientific_method",
          "paraphrase": "She articulates a method of proving things by experiment rather than conjecture.",
          "provenance": [
            {
              "backend": "anthropic",
              "normalization_notes": [
                "used bounded whitespace/typography/case fallback"
              ],
              "raw_id": "ev14",
              "source": "model",
              "source_chunk_id": null
            }
          ],
          "quote": "It is best to prove things by actual experiment; then you KNOW; whereas if you depend on guessing and supposing and conjecturing, you never get educated."
        },
        {
          "anchor": {
            "end_char": 27224,
            "paragraph_ids": [
              "p00063"
            ],
            "start_char": 27064
          },
          "confidence": 0.7,
          "entity_ids": [],
          "event_ids": [],
          "evidence_id": "sfev-46f126fb760fe6f8",
          "evidence_type": "inquiry_or_scientific_method",
          "paraphrase": "She describes repeated experimentation about whether water runs uphill.",
          "provenance": [
            {
              "backend": "anthropic",
              "normalization_notes": [
                "used bounded whitespace/typography/case fallback"
              ],
              "raw_id": "ev16",
              "source": "model",
              "source_chunk_id": null
            }
          ],
          "quote": "I have experimented and experimented until now I know it never does run uphill, except in the dark.  I know it does in the dark, because the pool never goes dry"
        },
        {
          "anchor": {
            "end_char": 28289,
            "paragraph_ids": [
              "p00065"
            ],
            "start_char": 28037
          },
          "confidence": 0.7,
          "entity_ids": [],
          "event_ids": [],
          "evidence_id": "sfev-5117c4c0d8b19b7e",
          "evidence_type": "inquiry_or_scientific_method",
          "paraphrase": "She reasons from cumulative evidence to a conclusion she cannot yet prove.",
          "provenance": [
            {
              "backend": "anthropic",
              "normalization_notes": [
                "used bounded whitespace/typography/case fallback"
              ],
              "raw_id": "ev15",
              "source": "model",
              "source_chunk_id": null
            }
          ],
          "quote": "By experiment I know that wood swims, and dry leaves, and feathers, and plenty of other things; therefore by all that cumulative evidence you know that a rock will swim; but you have to put up with simply knowing it, for there isn't any way to prove it"
        },
        {
          "anchor": {
            "end_char": 30162,
            "paragraph_ids": [
              "p00069"
            ],
            "start_char": 29996
          },
          "confidence": 0.6,
          "entity_ids": [],
          "event_ids": [],
          "evidence_id": "sfev-5e37e9b06bea932b",
          "evidence_type": "storyworld_change",
          "paraphrase": "After the Fall, the Garden is lost to her.",
          "provenance": [
            {
              "backend": "anthropic",
              "normalization_notes": [
                "used bounded whitespace/typography/case fallback"
              ],
              "raw_id": "ev20",
              "source": "model",
              "source_chunk_id": null
            }
          ],
          "quote": "When I look back, the Garden is a dream to me.  It was beautiful, surpassingly beautiful, enchantingly beautiful; and now it is lost, and I shall not see it any more."
        },
        {
          "anchor": {
            "end_char": 22748,
