          "evidence_id": "sfev-790eac6b9f2d7908",
          "evidence_type": "extrapolative_consequence",
          "paraphrase": "She reasons from observed shooting stars to the conclusion that all stars may one day vanish.",
          "provenance": [
            {
              "backend": "anthropic",
              "normalization_notes": [
                "used bounded whitespace/typography/case fallback"
              ],
              "raw_id": "ev18",
              "source": "model",
              "source_chunk_id": null
            }
          ],
          "quote": "By watching, I know that the stars are not going to last. I have seen some of the best ones melt and run down the sky. Since one can melt, they can all melt; since they can all melt, they can all melt the same night."
        },
        {
          "anchor": {
